Key findings.

\begin{enumerate}
    \item ACP matches Always Deliberate accuracy (0.992 vs 0.993) while deliberating only 64.6 percent of the time instead of 100 percent. This is a 35 percent reduction in average compute with no accuracy loss.
    \item Always Fast achieves high accuracy on easy inputs but Random Router collapses to 14 percent accuracy, showing that random routing is not a viable strategy.
    \item The routing accuracy of ACP is 95.4 percent, indicating the monitor learns to identify which inputs need deliberate processing.
    \item Easy deliberation rate (0.642) and hard deliberation rate (0.652) are nearly identical. This is an honest limitation: the synthetic task is easy enough that the fast pathway solves nearly everything, so there is little pressure to route differently by difficulty. Future work should use harder tasks where the fast pathway genuinely fails on hard inputs.
\end{enumerate}

